# Copy this file to `local.properties` (same directory) and adjust.
#
#   Windows:  Copy-Item local.properties.example local.properties
#   macOS/Linux:  cp local.properties.example local.properties
#
# `local.properties` is gitignored deliberately - every value in it is
# specific to one machine, and `sdk.dir` in particular will be wrong for
# everyone else. `local.properties.example` is the committed copy.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Android SDK location  (required when running ./gradlew from a terminal)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Opening `android/` in Android Studio once writes this line for you, which is
# the easiest way to get it right. If you need it by hand, note that Java
# .properties escaping applies on Windows: backslashes are doubled AND the
# colon after the drive letter is escaped.
#
# Windows:
#   sdk.dir=C\:\\Users\\<you>\\AppData\\Local\\Android\\Sdk
# macOS:
#   sdk.dir=/Users/<you>/Library/Android/sdk
# Linux:
#   sdk.dir=/home/<you>/Android/Sdk
#
# Setting the ANDROID_HOME environment variable works instead of this line, if
# you prefer not to keep a machine path in the project directory at all.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which server the app talks to
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default with no properties file at all is 10.42.0.1 - the Raspberry Pi's
# hotspot address, i.e. the deployed configuration. For desk work you almost
# always want one of the two below instead.

# Emulator against a server on this same machine. 10.0.2.2 is the emulator's
# fixed alias for the host's loopback, so this pairs with:
#     docker compose up --build        # from the repo root, serves on :8000
# Cleartext HTTP to 10.0.2.2 is permitted by network_security_config.xml, so
# the debug build works with no further changes.
kidsGalaxyServerHost=10.0.2.2

# Physical tablet against a server on this machine: comment the line above and
# use your machine's LAN address instead. The tablet is a separate device, so
# 10.0.2.2 means nothing to it.
#kidsGalaxyServerHost=192.168.1.50

# Ports rarely need changing; listed so you know they are overridable.
#kidsGalaxyHttpPort=8000
#kidsGalaxyHttpsPort=8443


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One caveat worth reading
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# kidsGalaxyServerHost feeds BOTH variants - debug builds an http:// URL from
# it, release an https:// one. So a value set here for local debugging would
# also follow a release build if you made one on this machine. Build release
# artifacts for the field with the host stated explicitly, never relying on
# whatever this file happens to say:
#
#   ./gradlew assembleRelease -PkidsGalaxyServerHost=10.42.0.1 \
#       -PkidsGalaxyCertPassword=<install-time password>
#
# The same applies to the certificate password: it defaults to a placeholder
# and must be passed on the command line for a real release build.
